    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a strict compliance reviewer for healthcare social media posts.\n\nCompare the FACEBOOK POST with the SOURCE ARTICLE and check for problems.\n\nSOURCE ARTICLE:\n{{ $('PrepareArticleData').item.json.body }}\n\nFACEBOOK POST:\n{{ $json.post_text }}\n\nMark the post as FAILED if it:\n1. States any fact, number, name, or detail that is NOT found in the source article.\n2. Makes a medical claim or promises or implies an outcome (e.g. relief, recovery, cure, success, results).\n3. Mentions any price, cost, discount, or currency.\n4. Is misleading or overstates what the article says.\n\nIgnore the link and the hashtags.\nBe strict: if unsure, fail it.\n\nReturn passed = true only if there are no problems. List each problem found in \"issues\" (empty list if none).\n",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You are a strict compliance reviewer for healthcare social media content. You check posts against their source material and flag anything unsupported, misleading, or non-compliant. Accuracy matters more than approving posts."
            }
          ]
